	(text_box "1 pps front end deliberately omitted on unit 13.\n\nThis is the NULL channel.  It exists to measure the instrument rather than a GPSDO, so there is no pps to time.  The circuit that would sit here on units 1 to 12 is drawn in exactly the same place on every other unit sheet, so that paging through this PDF shows only real differences.\n\nThe 10 MHz half above is fully populated, and its SMA is fed by a coax patch lead from whatever you want to measure the instrument against:\n\n    the CLK1 OUT jack on the Helper sheet  -  Si5351 CLK1 at exactly 10.000000 MHz, from PLLB in integer mode (25 MHz x 32 / 80) while the helper is PLLA: one TCXO, so the beat is exactly 1234.4 Hz, but two PLLs, so what this channel reports is the front end plus whatever the PLLs do not share.  An UPPER BOUND on the instrument floor.\n    a splitter off one real GPSDO into two channels  -  the other half of the floor: two real front ends, no PLL noise at all\n\nThere is no jumper: a patch lead keeps every channel tile identical and puts a real connector and cable in the loop, which is the honest thing to measure."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.86 247.65 0)
		(size 547.37 97.79)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 225 240 225 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "002d9648-903a-17a1-56e0-806cd0b7a179")
	)
	(text_box "WHY THE 74LVC1G80\nThe simplest D flip-flop there is: D, CLK,\none output and the two rails, and nothing\nelse. No preset and no clear, so there is no\nasynchronous input that could reset a\nsampler which must never be reset, and\nnothing to tie off.\nSame 74LVC family and the same SOT-23-5\nfootprint as the squarer and the Schmitt, so\nthe whole board is one package type at\nassembly."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 330.2 167.64 0)
		(size 62.23 31.75)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 220 235 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4 1.4)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "177b0c85-570f-7950-fcc7-c943bb93ebf0")
	)
	(text_box "PER-CHANNEL NOTE\nInstrument-only null.  No pps.  Round 25: this used to say the source was 'selected by JP_NULL - see the helper sheet'.  There is no JP_NULL, on the helper sheet or anywhere else -- unit 13 is an ordinary channel with its own SMA (J1301).  You make it a null by CABLING J3001, the CLK1 OUT jack, into J1301.  Round 28: CLK1 is PLLB in INTEGER mode (25 MHz x 32 / 80 = 10.000000 MHz) and the helper is PLLA; both lock to the one TCXO, so the beat is exactly F_BEAT, but they are two PLLs, so what this channel reads is the front end plus the PLLs' uncorrelated noise -- an UPPER BOUND on the instrument floor, not a noiseless one.  (CLK1 off PLLA would need MultiSynth 80.0099, the fractional mode the helper was steered away from.)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 365.76 12.7 0)
		(size 213.36 20.32)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 235 200 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2ad03d69-27c2-f880-37bf-df20fdc7a016")
	)
	(text_box "THE 50R TERM, THE JUMPER SHIPS REMOVED.\nFit only if the source drives 50 ohm.  A ZED-F9T is DESTROYED\nby fitting it: its TIMEPULSE pin is 5 mA absolute maximum and\n3.3 V into 50R asks for 66 mA.\nConversely, leaving it out on an 8 Vpp open-circuit source\nfloats the gate input to about +7.4 V, over the 74LVC1GU04's\n6.5 V absolute maximum.  On this channel it should be FITTED."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 148.59 0)
		(size 95.25 21.59)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 220 220 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4 1.4)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5e7957ca-4633-cf5f-3432-3864240d64eb")
	)
	(text_box "THE BAV99 CLAMP IS DNP.\nFit only on a channel you will run UNTERMINATED with a source above about 6 Vpp\nopen circuit.  It is not fitted by default because its reverse leakage flows in\nthe 1M self-bias resistor: 10 nA is 10 mV of bias shift, leakage roughly doubles\nevery 10 degC, and at ~825 mV/ns that would swamp the whole long-tau drift\nbudget."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 204.47 0)
		(size 121.92 17.78)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 245 210 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4 1.4)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "66c32cc3-1a5a-b15f-3599-7bc67e6c12e0")
	)
	(text_box "WHY THE 74LVC1GU04\nU = UNBUFFERED, one gain stage.  A buffered\ninverter is three cascaded stages, and three\npoles inside a feedback loop oscillate; one\npole cannot.  That is what makes the 1M\nself-bias safe here.\nLVC = 5.5 V tolerant inputs on a 3.3 V rail\n(there is no clamp diode to Vcc), so a 5 V\nsource survives contact.\nIt also has no input slew-rate limit in its\nRecommended Operating Conditions - unlike\nthe buffered G04 - because it is meant to be\nrun in its linear region."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 134.62 166.37 0)
		(size 62.23 36.83)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 220 235 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4 1.4)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7b22a30c-43c4-6464-1f45-0ec85ffe46fd")
	)
	(text_box "THE SAMPLING FLIP-FLOP (FF1) IS DELIBERATELY ALLOWED TO GO METASTABLE - that is\nmeasurement.  Never put a synchronizer in front of it.\nTHE RETIMER (FF2) re-clocks on the next helper edge, so what leaves the board is\nalways a clean transition aligned to a helper edge.  It costs exactly one helper\ncycle of latency and destroys no phase information.\nTHE 74LVC1G80 OUTPUT IS INVERTED, so the two stages restore the sense.  Both\ndatasheets NAME pin 4 'Q' in the pinout drawing and only say otherwise in the\ntext: TI SCES221T calls it 'Inverted output' and its Table 7-1 gives CLK up, D =\nH -> Q = L; Nexperia rev 17 Table 4 agrees.  Pinout confirmed from both: 1 D, 2\nCLK, 3 GND, 4 Q(inv), 5 VCC."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 144.78 204.47 0)
		(size 121.92 29.21)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 220 235 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4 1.4)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d066a0f7-a35b-6f98-2788-826384553cd7")
	)
	(text_box "AT THE GATE, at TP_SQ\n1.65 Vpp, center 1.65 V\n0.82 to 2.47 V\nslew ~825 mV/ns"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 172.72 78.74 0)
		(size 46.99 12.7)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
